.TH IPHONE-MIRROR-BRIDGE-UI 1 "2026" "iphone-mirror-bridge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iphone-mirror-bridge-ui \- desktop app for iPhone Mirror Bridge
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iphone-mirror-bridge-ui
[\fB\-\-tray\fR|\fB\-\-connect\fR|\fB\-\-settings\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows the iPhone's screen (AirPlay, through UxPlay) in a window with a device
frame and toolbar, and controls the iPhone through the
\fBiphone-mirror-bridge\fR service: click the screen to hand the touchpad and
keyboard to the iPhone, press Ctrl+F8 to take them back. The toolbar has Home
and App Switcher buttons. A system tray icon shows the connection state.
.PP
The Connect window shows the 6-digit code the iPhone asks for when pairing in
its Bluetooth settings. Settings covers display, controls, notifications,
paired devices and privacy.
.PP
Only one copy runs per user; starting it again brings up its window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Start in the system tray without opening a window (used at login).
.TP
.B \-\-connect
Open the Connect iPhone window.
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Open Settings.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/iphone-mirror-bridge/ui.json
display and notification preferences.
.br
.I /var/lib/iphone-mirror-bridge/settings.json
control settings, kept by the service.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iphone-mirror-bridge (1),
.BR iphone-mirror-screen (1)
